@node MAIN "BitSkim 0.1 - AmigaOS manual"

                         @{b}BitSkim 0.1@{ub}
                 Different generations. Same network.

 Disk-backed queues send one file at a time. Browse the whole list
 with Previous/Next; approve once and choose one folder.
 Choose Accept all and one destination folder for that listed batch.
 Main progress shows one bar, the current filename, amounts and speed.
 The bar starts afresh for every file. The outgoing waiting count appears
 below it. Negotiated batches show 1/2, 2/2 etc. for sending and receiving.
 Older single-file offers have no remote batch total.
 Hold the right mouse button for the Queue menu: Continue/Retry,
 Pause after file, Skip idle file and Clear waiting. There is no extra
 queue window or clickable progress row.

 @{"Quick start" link "QUICKSTART"}        @{"Requirements" link "REQUIREMENTS"}
 @{"Installation" link "INSTALL"}       @{"Find a computer" link "DISCOVERY"}
 @{"Send a file" link "SENDING"}        @{"Receive a file" link "RECEIVING"}
 @{"Transfer tools" link "TOOLS"}     @{"Folders and disk space" link "FOLDERS"}
 @{"Collection results and retry" link "RESULTS"}
